// Phase 2f (issue #1115): a procedure with an out-of-line `proof ... end`
// block supplies proof slots cited by `by <slot>` clauses. Installing those
// slot bindings into the proof environment is out of scope for this slice
// (proof slots are a later slice), so a procedure that declares one is
// deferred rather than verified -- otherwise discharging `assert x = x by
// slot` would report `slot` as an undefined proof variable. The Phase 1m
// "accepted but not verified" warning (issue #1108) fires instead, pinned by
// the `.pf.warn` sibling under both parsers. An inline `assert P by <proof>`
// with no proof block is still verified (see `proc_verify.pf`).
proc slotted(x: bool)
{
  assert x = x by slot
}
proof
  slot { . }
end
